# Production AWS frontend env template — DO NOT USE YET

This file is a **cutover-readiness placeholder**. It is not loaded by Vite.

- Do **not** copy this over `.env.production` until a human approves production cutover.
- Do **not** point it at the **staging** Cognito pool (`us-east-1_vPmQ7cL1F`) or staging API.
- Do **not** put RDS passwords, AWS keys, or provider secrets in any `VITE_*` variable.
- Production provider execution stays disabled on the API (`AWS_PROVIDER_EXECUTION_ENABLED=false`) even after the SPA switches.

Production `.env.production` remains the live Lovable/Supabase build until DNS cutover.

```
# Uncomment only on an approved production AWS frontend deploy.
# VITE_AUTH_PROVIDER=cognito
# VITE_APP_URL=https://checksops.com
# VITE_CHECKSOPS_API_URL=https://REPLACE-WITH-PRODUCTION-API-GATEWAY/prod
# VITE_AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=REPLACE-WITH-PRODUCTION-POOL
# VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_CLIENT_ID=REPLACE-WITH-PRODUCTION-CLIENT
```

Cognito WebAuthn RP ID must match the production pool (`checksops.com` if that is the canonical host). Staging passkeys do not transfer.

Plaid is not required. Leave Plaid disabled on the API.
